█  VERTEBRATE ORIGIN CHAIN                  
█  (fish → amphibian → reptile → mammal)         

   FISH (fins, cold‑blooded)
        │
        ▼
   SALAMANDER‑LIKE AMPHIBIANS
   (legs from fins, cold‑blooded)
        │
        ▼
   EARLY REPTILES
   (legs, scales, cold‑blooded)
        │
        ▼
   MAMMAL‑SIDE REPTILES
   (pelycosaurs → the FIN‑BACKS)
        │
        │   ┌───────────────────────────────┐
        ▼   ▼                               │
   FIN‑BACKS (Dimetrodon-type)
   - NOT fish fins
   - NOT dinosaurs
   - Skin sail on backbone spines
   - PARTLY warm‑blooded
   - First step toward mammal metabolism
        │
        ▼
   THERAPSIDS
   (advanced mammal‑like reptiles,
    more warm‑blooded, fur starting)
        │
        ▼
   CYNODONTS
   (proto‑mammals: fully warm‑blooded,
    whiskers, fur, milk glands)
        │
        ▼
   EARLY MAMMALS
   (warm‑blooded, egg‑laying)
        │
        ▼
   MODERN MAMMALS
   (egg‑laying → pouch → placental)
